  "title": "What if you could see Wi-Fi?",
  "series": "Field Study / The Dead Spot",
  "pacing": "micro",
  "narration": "You walk closer to the router and somehow your Wi-Fi gets worse. Look at your feet. You just stepped into a dead spot. If you could see Wi-Fi, you'd see one wave coming straight from the router to your phone. But that metal cabinet bounces another copy your way. Same signal, longer trip. Right here, the peak of one wave meets the dip of the other, so they partly cancel. Now slide your phone a few inches. The waves line up differently and the signal climbs. You didn't fix the router. You just moved your hand.",
